Tessera BYO ingest demo corpus (Milestone 18, spec 0120 / ADR 0029).

A small, self-assembled corpus of PUBLIC-DOMAIN factual data about five U.S.
cities and four regions — city name, state, approximate population, founding
year, and region — plus a short Markdown note. The facts (populations rounded,
founding dates, state capitals) are commonly published public information; this
assembly carries no third-party copyright and is distributed under the same MIT
license as the rest of the repository.

Its purpose is to demonstrate `tessera ingest <dir>` on committed, reproducible
data: two CSV tables joined by a foreign key, a Markdown document linked by
mention, multi-field entity resolution, and — deliberately — an ambiguous name
("Portland" refers to two distinct cities, Oregon and Maine), so the
"ambiguous names refuse" contract can be shown end to end.
